AICSemi AIC8800D80 USB staging driver
=====================================

Source: https://github.com/radxa-pkg/aic8800
Release: 5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-7
Commit: 6e07604

This directory contains the USB Wi-Fi portions of Radxa's AIC8800 package
needed for the AIC8800D80 on the Radxa ROCK 4D:

  src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw
  src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv

Before import, every patch listed in Radxa's debian/patches/series was applied
in release order. Legacy line endings and trailing whitespace were normalized.
The resulting source was integrated under drivers/staging with kernel-native
Kconfig and Kbuild files. The DKMS packaging and standalone platform build
logic were not imported.

Licensing provenance
--------------------

COPYRIGHT.radxa.original is a byte-for-byte copy of Radxa's debian/copyright.
Its Files patterns refer to paths in Radxa's original package, not paths in
this kernel tree.

The imported driver directories originated below src/USB/driver_fw and are
therefore covered by the original src/* paragraph, which Radxa declares
GPL-2. Changes flattened from debian/patches/* are declared by Radxa to use
the same license as the source they modify. This records Radxa's package
metadata; it does not claim that Radxa authored every imported vendor file.

Flipper-specific changes after flattening:

- Replaced standalone/DKMS and platform Makefiles with in-tree Kbuild.
- Added Linux 7.2 cfg80211 remain-on-channel compatibility.
- Replaced removed unsafe string operations used by Linux 7.2 builds.

This is an incubation import, not an upstream-ready driver. See TODO for the
remaining scope reduction, subsystem integration, and firmware provenance work.
